-Everything!

525
00:16:14,307 --> 00:16:16,310
-You are wrong, Winky-breath.

526
00:16:16,343 --> 00:16:18,545
-I grant you one hour
to leave Ophecius.

527
00:16:18,578 --> 00:16:19,212
-One hour?

528
00:16:19,245 --> 00:16:20,413
Crap, we're not even packed.

529
00:16:20,447 --> 00:16:23,217
-If you don't, you and your
spaceship will be destroyed.

530
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:25,252
-You and your
daughter are doomed.

531
00:16:25,285 --> 00:16:28,188
-Only 59 minutes remain.

532
00:16:28,222 --> 00:16:31,192
Lasvon, train the guns
on their spaceship.

533
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:35,262
59 minutes.

534
00:16:35,295 --> 00:16:36,630
-A CBS News magazine.

535
00:16:36,663 --> 00:16:38,298
-Come on, Rocky, Winky.

536
00:16:38,332 --> 00:16:39,733
It's useless.

537
00:16:39,767 --> 00:16:43,070
We're wasting our
precious minutes.

538
00:16:43,103 --> 00:16:46,440
-"The Honeymooners!"

539
00:16:46,473 --> 00:16:47,742
-Well, we had plenty
of time to spare.

540
00:16:47,775 --> 00:16:51,545
We could have hit the
gift shop or something.

541
00:16:51,578 --> 00:16:53,347
-Boy, oh, boy.

542
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:55,115
-It's pretty slow for a rocket.

543
00:16:58,652 --> 00:17:00,387
-Ah, Cleolanta.

544
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:02,288
A stubborn woman
if I ever saw one.

545
00:17:02,322 --> 00:17:03,288
-You've never see one, Rocky.

546
00:17:03,322 --> 00:17:04,725
-You can't argue with
self-sufficient people

547
00:17:04,758 --> 00:17:05,592
like that.

548
00:17:05,625 --> 00:17:07,627
-Well, now me, I--
I'm a family guy.

549
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:08,460
I like my neighbors.

550
00:17:08,493 --> 00:17:11,098
You know, how about
a game of cards.

551
00:17:11,132 --> 00:17:12,598
Or may I borrow a cup of sugar?

552
00:17:12,632 --> 00:17:13,567
-Can I see your butt?

553
00:17:16,237 --> 00:17:18,205
-Orbit Jet to
Space Station OW-9.

554
00:17:22,642 --> 00:17:23,242
[BEEPING]

555
00:17:23,275 --> 00:17:24,478
-Won't Rocky be surprised?

556
00:17:24,512 --> 00:17:27,447
-When I tell him I'm pregnant!

557
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:30,350
Station OW-9 to Orbit Jet.

558
00:17:30,383 --> 00:17:31,752
Andrews to Rocky Jones.

559
00:17:31,785 --> 00:17:32,418
Come in, Rocky.

560
00:17:32,452 --> 00:17:33,052
-Hm?

561
00:17:33,085 --> 00:17:34,855
I'm using my space voice.

562
00:17:34,888 --> 00:17:36,590
-OW-9 to Orbit Jet.

563
00:17:36,623 --> 00:17:38,358
Come in, Rocky Jones.

564
00:17:38,392 --> 00:17:39,693
-Well, what's the
matter with Andrews?

565
00:17:39,727 --> 00:17:41,528
Has he got a mouth full
of crackers, or something?

566
00:17:41,562 --> 00:17:43,797
-No, he's got an
extra Y chromosome.

567
00:17:43,830 --> 00:17:45,732
-Rocket Jones to OW-9.

568
00:17:45,765 --> 00:17:47,700
Come in, OW-9.

569
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:49,335
Andrews to Rocky Jones.

570
00:17:49,368 --> 00:17:49,870
Come in.

571
00:17:49,903 --> 00:17:50,837
-Heh, heh.

572
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:53,407
[CHUCKLING]

573
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:54,207
-Goodness, gracious!

574
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,475
-Great balls of fire!

575
00:17:58,478 --> 00:18:01,748
-That's Professor Newton,
and Vina and Bobby.

576
00:18:01,782 --> 00:18:02,682
-That's right, Winky.

577
00:18:02,715 --> 00:18:03,683
We're all here.

578
00:18:03,717 --> 00:18:04,718
-And this is "Your Life."

579
00:18:04,752 --> 00:18:07,453
-Say, what are you doing
on Space Station OW-9?

580
00:18:07,487 --> 00:18:09,255
-Oh, we're having
a Mary Kay party.

581
00:18:09,288 --> 00:18:12,525
-We're here to greet old
friends, Rocky-- Potonda,

582
00:18:12,558 --> 00:18:14,928
Bavarro, and Torvak.

583
00:18:14,962 --> 00:18:15,995
-What?

584
00:18:16,028 --> 00:18:17,998
Did they manage to build
a spaceship of their own?

585
00:18:18,032 --> 00:18:19,767
-Winky, honey, hang up the line.

586
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,935
-The Gypsy Moons,
Posita and Nagato,

587
00:18:21,968 --> 00:18:23,770
are entering our solar system.

588
00:18:23,803 --> 00:18:25,037
Placenta and Neg--

589
00:18:25,070 --> 00:18:30,610
-And at 0600 today, they will be
very close this space station.

590
00:18:30,643 --> 00:18:32,245
-Not close enough to wave.

591
00:18:32,278 --> 00:18:34,480
But close enough to dock.

592
00:18:34,513 --> 00:18:35,315
-Professor Newton--

593
00:18:35,348 --> 00:18:36,582
-Please hit Bobby.

594
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:39,953
-Where will the space station be
in relation to the Gypsy Moons?

595
00:18:39,987 --> 00:18:42,622
-Directly between them, Rocky.

596
00:18:42,655 --> 00:18:43,390
-Andrews?

597
00:18:43,423 --> 00:18:44,190
-Hm?

598
00:18:44,223 --> 00:18:46,393
-Yes, Rocky, great
news, isn't it?

599
00:18:46,427 --> 00:18:47,260
-Stand by.

600
00:18:47,293 --> 00:18:48,562
I'll check back as
soon as possible.

601
00:18:48,595 --> 00:18:49,228
Out.

602
00:18:49,262 --> 00:18:50,697
Winky, stay at the controls.

603
00:18:50,730 --> 00:18:51,363
Correct direction.

604
00:18:51,397 --> 00:18:52,765
Head for Space Station OW-9.

605
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:53,800
-I gotta go potty.

606
00:18:57,337 --> 00:18:58,872
-OK, let's see how
we start this here.

607
00:18:58,905 --> 00:19:01,675
Uh-- Dear Abby, I'm
an elderly woman

608
00:19:01,708 --> 00:19:03,677
who doesn't enjoy sex anymore.

609
00:19:03,710 --> 00:19:05,345
I found that in the--

610
00:19:05,378 --> 00:19:06,780
What is it, Rocky?

611
00:19:06,813 --> 00:19:09,883
-Something Professor Newton
overlooked-- the atmosphere

612
00:19:09,917 --> 00:19:12,485
chain which links the two moons.

613
00:19:12,518 --> 00:19:15,422
Now assume this is
the space station.

614
00:19:15,455 --> 00:19:16,857
-And this is the ship
arriving too late

615
00:19:16,890 --> 00:19:17,923
to save a drowning witch.

616
00:19:17,957 --> 00:19:19,993
-And these are the Gypsy
Moons, Posita and Nagato--

617
00:19:20,027 --> 00:19:20,827
-Hm.

618
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:22,362
- --approaching
from that direction.

619
00:19:22,395 --> 00:19:22,963
-Neat.

620
00:19:22,997 --> 00:19:24,430
-Now as the moons pass--

621
00:19:24,463 --> 00:19:25,663
-Mm, hm.

622
00:19:25,697 --> 00:19:27,400
- --the atmosphere chain will
envelope the space station.

623
00:19:27,433 --> 00:19:27,968
-Oh!
Neat.

624
00:19:28,002 --> 00:19:28,835
Funny.

625
00:19:28,868 --> 00:19:30,137
-It was built only
to stand in space.

626
00:19:30,170 --> 00:19:31,203
-Cute.

627
00:19:31,237 --> 00:19:33,373
-A sudden whoosh of
atmosphere could destroy it.

628
00:19:33,407 --> 00:19:33,773
-Wonderful.

629
00:19:33,807 --> 00:19:34,573
Mm, hm.

630
00:19:34,607 --> 00:19:35,708
-Where are we in
relation to them?

631
00:19:35,742 --> 00:19:37,443
-This is out position, here.

632
00:19:37,477 --> 00:19:38,443
-Next to that TCBY.

633
00:19:38,477 --> 00:19:40,047
-I don't know whether we
can reach Space Station

634
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:43,150
OW-9 in time to evacuate it.

635
00:19:43,183 --> 00:19:44,383
-I'll try to make reservations.

636
00:19:49,088 --> 00:19:51,592
-I can't understand
Rocky not being excited

637
00:19:51,625 --> 00:19:53,460
about the Gypsy Moons.

638
00:19:53,493 --> 00:19:56,028
-Maybe Mr. Secretary
put the pressure on him.

639
00:19:56,062 --> 00:19:58,032
Perhaps he didn't like
our blasting off Earth

640
00:19:58,065 --> 00:19:58,898
without orders.

641
00:19:58,932 --> 00:20:00,100
-Maybe he thinks
he's too good for us.

642
00:20:00,133 --> 00:20:02,068
Well, screw, Rocky.

643
00:20:02,102 --> 00:20:04,070
-Well, I can't think
of any other reason.

644
00:20:04,103 --> 00:20:06,707
[BEEPING]

645
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:09,943
-Orbit Jet to
Space Station OW-9.

646
00:20:09,977 --> 00:20:10,943
Rocky Jones to Andrews.

647
00:20:10,977 --> 00:20:12,112
Come in Andrews.

648
00:20:12,145 --> 00:20:12,712
-Yes, Rocky?

649
00:20:12,745 --> 00:20:13,645
-Whoa!

650
00:20:13,678 --> 00:20:14,480
Got enough Maybelline
on there, Skipper?

651
00:20:14,513 --> 00:20:15,982
-Give me your
refueling schedule.

652
00:20:16,015 --> 00:20:17,985
When's the next spaceship due?

653
00:20:18,018 --> 00:20:19,218
-I'm having a
Monteclaire moment.

654
00:20:19,252 --> 00:20:20,218
-Nothing scheduled, Rocky.

655
00:20:20,252 --> 00:20:23,123
Since Transport TR-14
left, we're all clear.

656
00:20:23,157 --> 00:20:24,190
-I'll sing off.

657
00:20:24,223 --> 00:20:25,658
Call back the TR-14.

658
00:20:25,692 --> 00:20:26,592
Bring it back.

659
00:20:26,625 --> 00:20:28,228
-And back-fill the
story for the audience.

660
00:20:28,262 --> 00:20:29,663
They have no idea
what's going on.

661
00:20:29,697 --> 00:20:30,163
-What is it Rocky?

662
00:20:30,197 --> 00:20:31,765
What's the matter?

663
00:20:31,798 --> 00:20:34,000
-I have to clear
for Andrews' call.

664
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:37,170
Just remind Professor Newton
of the atmosphere chain.

665
00:20:37,203 --> 00:20:38,038
-And hurry, Andrews.

666
00:20:38,072 --> 00:20:39,072
Make the call.

667
00:20:39,105 --> 00:20:40,107
Bring back but the TR-14.

668
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:41,542
-Bring back the Boston Rag!

669
00:20:41,575 --> 00:20:43,643
-The atmosphere
chain, Professor?

670
00:20:43,677 --> 00:20:45,978
-The atmosphere chain.

671
00:20:46,012 --> 00:20:49,182
Now, what can Rocky have m--

672
00:20:49,215 --> 00:20:50,683
-Oh, I've soiled myself again.

673
00:20:50,717 --> 00:20:51,117
-Of course!

674
00:20:51,150 --> 00:20:51,918
Of course!

675
00:20:51,952 --> 00:20:52,452
Oh!

676
00:20:52,485 --> 00:20:53,653
-He's a queer duck!

677
00:20:53,687 --> 00:20:54,688
-How stupid of me.

678
00:20:54,722 --> 00:20:56,757
-What is it, Professor?

679
00:20:56,790 --> 00:20:57,223
-Yes, what?

680
00:20:57,257 --> 00:20:58,257
-What?

681
00:20:58,290 --> 00:21:01,093
-Quick Andrews, make
your call, as Rocky said.

682
00:21:01,127 --> 00:21:04,097
Space Station OW-9
to Transport TR-14.

683
00:21:04,130 --> 00:21:05,965
Come in, TR-14, come in.

684
00:21:05,998 --> 00:21:06,567
-Hm?

685
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:07,600
Hm.

686
00:21:07,633 --> 00:21:08,935
-Vladimir Horowitz.

687
00:21:08,968 --> 00:21:10,270
-I've made a terrible blunder.

688
00:21:10,303 --> 00:21:10,903
I've--

689
00:21:10,937 --> 00:21:11,837
-I'll say.

690
00:21:11,870 --> 00:21:13,207
- --led you and Bobby
into grave peril.

691
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:14,908
-I don't care.

692
00:21:14,942 --> 00:21:15,708
-Aah!

693
00:21:15,742 --> 00:21:18,112
-The OW-9 is going
to be destroyed!

694
00:21:18,145 --> 00:21:19,078
[GULP]

695
00:21:19,112 --> 00:21:21,280
-What do you mean, Professor?

696
00:21:21,313 --> 00:21:24,818
-An object built to withstand
the elements of space

697
00:21:24,852 --> 00:21:27,287
cannot survive in an atmosphere!

698
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:28,120
-Oh, like you know that!

699
00:21:28,153 --> 00:21:30,823
-The atmosphere
chain, that's right!

700
00:21:30,857 --> 00:21:31,790
-Yep, I--

701
00:21:31,823 --> 00:21:34,127
-And Rocky wants the
TR-14 to evacuate us.

702
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:34,728
-Ugh!

703
00:21:34,762 --> 00:21:35,995
-Ick!

704
00:21:36,028 --> 00:21:40,333
-Space Station OW-9 to Transport
TR-14, urgent, repeat urgent!

705
00:21:40,367 --> 00:21:42,635
Come in.

706
00:21:42,668 --> 00:21:43,737
I can't get an answer.

707
00:21:43,770 --> 00:21:45,372
Shall I call Rocky back?

708
00:21:45,405 --> 00:21:46,807
-He knows what's happening.

709
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:48,308
He'll do everything possible.

710
00:21:48,342 --> 00:21:50,210
Keep trying the TR-14.

711
00:21:50,243 --> 00:21:51,412
-And keep reaching
for the stars!

712
00:21:51,445 --> 00:21:54,180
-OW-9 to TR-14, come in.

713
00:21:54,213 --> 00:21:54,915
Mayday!

714
00:21:54,948 --> 00:21:56,883
Repeat, Mayday!

715
00:21:56,917 --> 00:22:01,455
Space Station OW-9 to
Transport TR-14, mayday!

716
00:22:01,488 --> 00:22:02,655
Repeat, mayday!

717
00:22:02,688 --> 00:22:04,925
-Um, do you fellas have a
chair I could on, or something?

718
00:22:04,958 --> 00:22:07,993
-I'm bleeding her now, Rocky,
all the thrust she's got.

719
00:22:08,027 --> 00:22:09,127
-Jeez.

720
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:12,465
-Space Station OW-9 to Transport
TR-14, can you hear me?

721
00:22:12,498 --> 00:22:13,433
Turn back!

722
00:22:13,467 --> 00:22:15,968
Turn back!

723
00:22:16,002 --> 00:22:16,802
-I resent that!

724
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:19,338
-Orbit Jet to
Space Station OW-9.

725
00:22:19,372 --> 00:22:21,007
Rocky Jones to Andrews.

726
00:22:21,040 --> 00:22:22,408
-Yes, Rocky?

727
00:22:22,442 --> 00:22:23,877
-It's no use, Andrews.

728
00:22:23,910 --> 00:22:25,145
The TR-14 is beyond reach.

729
00:22:25,178 --> 00:22:26,980
-So deal with it, man.

730
00:22:27,013 --> 00:22:29,015
-Has Professor Newton
rechecked his figures?

731
00:22:29,048 --> 00:22:29,815
-Hm?

732
00:22:29,848 --> 00:22:30,717
-Have you checked
his credentials?

733
00:22:30,750 --> 00:22:31,918
-Yes, Rocky.

734
00:22:31,952 --> 00:22:33,153
And their absolute.

735
00:22:33,187 --> 00:22:34,387
- --ly.

736
00:22:34,420 --> 00:22:40,527
-The Gypsy Moons will pass the
space station at 0600 today.

737
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,363
-Don't worry, we'll get
you off before then.

738
00:22:43,397 --> 00:22:44,197
-All right!

739
00:22:44,230 --> 00:22:46,232
Heh, heh.

740
00:22:46,265 --> 00:22:48,835
-Tell Andrews I'll call
back every hour on the hour.

741
00:22:48,868 --> 00:22:51,438
-Then I start
tossing out bodies.

742
00:22:51,472 --> 00:22:53,807
-Please, try to understand--

743
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:54,440
-I'm a magic man.

744
00:22:54,473 --> 00:22:55,242
-(SINGING) A dun-dun, chh!

745
00:22:55,275 --> 00:22:57,543
A dun-dun hoo!

746
00:22:57,577 --> 00:23:00,147
- --but seeing out friends
on the Gypsy Moons.

747
00:23:00,180 --> 00:23:01,548
-My entire life is a lie.

748
00:23:01,582 --> 00:23:03,850
-Oh, the Gypsy Moons.

749
00:23:03,883 --> 00:23:05,118
-The Gypsy Moons, huh?

750
00:23:05,152 --> 00:23:07,453
-Hey, that's a novel idea.

751
00:23:07,487 --> 00:23:08,322
-Have you a plan, Rocky?

752
00:23:08,355 --> 00:23:09,522
Something we can do?

753
00:23:09,555 --> 00:23:20,567
Leaving the space station
before 0600 looks impossible.

754
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:21,500
-Ha, ha.

755
00:23:21,533 --> 00:23:23,503
Oh, I hope you're
enjoying today's film.

756
00:23:23,537 --> 00:23:26,540
And I certainly hope those
Gypsy Moons don't crash.

757
00:23:26,573 --> 00:23:28,475
Did you know that the
Gypsy Moons is actually

758
00:23:28,508 --> 00:23:31,578
a reference to a popular
song title from the 1920s?

759
00:23:31,612 --> 00:23:32,578
Mm, hm.

760
00:23:32,612 --> 00:23:33,478
Don't remember?

761
00:23:33,512 --> 00:23:36,015
Well, here's our own
Tom Servo, Gypsy,

762
00:23:36,048 --> 00:23:38,318
and Crow to help you out,
doing their rendition

763
00:23:38,352 --> 00:23:39,385
of "The Gypsy Moons."

764
00:23:39,418 --> 00:23:40,587
Hit it kids.

765
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:44,023
-Oh, I'm telling ya
Gypsy, I love you.

766
00:23:44,057 --> 00:23:45,558
And I know I'd love you
too, if only we could--

767
00:23:45,592 --> 00:23:48,127
-Why, you haven't a chance
with a girl like her.

768
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:49,662
It's me she cares for.

769
00:23:49,695 --> 00:23:51,063
Isn't that right, Gypsy?

770
00:23:51,097 --> 00:23:52,098
-I can't decide.

771
00:23:52,132 --> 00:23:53,433
Can't decide?

772
00:23:53,467 --> 00:23:54,500
Well, maybe this will help.

773
00:23:54,533 --> 00:23:55,535
[STRUMMING BANJO AND WHISTLING]

774
00:23:58,605 --> 00:23:59,940
-Ba-boom, ba-boom.

775
00:23:59,973 --> 00:24:03,108
-(SINGING) I can't
sleep, or clean my room,

776
00:24:03,142 --> 00:24:07,413
[WHISTLING] since you and I
first had our swoony swoon.

777
00:24:07,447 --> 00:24:08,613
-Ooh!

778
00:24:08,647 --> 00:24:12,585
-(SINGING) In early June under
the clear blue Gypsy Moon.

779
00:24:12,618 --> 00:24:13,287
-Ooh, that's nice.

780
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:14,187
-No, no, no.

781
00:24:14,220 --> 00:24:15,288
Don't listen to him, honey.

782
00:24:15,322 --> 00:24:16,055
Listen to me.

783
00:24:16,088 --> 00:24:16,922
-I should.

784
00:24:16,955 --> 00:24:18,258
(SINGING)- While
others have their tune,

785
00:24:18,292 --> 00:24:20,393
I know that I was meant for you.

786
00:24:20,427 --> 00:24:21,260
-Ooh.

787
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:22,195
-(SINGING) Yes one
on one makes two,

788
00:24:22,228 --> 00:24:24,330
