1046
00:33:03,582 --> 00:33:06,418
-Well, when a man and a woman
love each other very much--

1047
00:33:06,452 --> 00:33:08,620
- --travel around the sun.

1048
00:33:08,653 --> 00:33:11,423
-And the Gypsy Moons
travel around each other.

1049
00:33:11,457 --> 00:33:13,092
-Exactly, Rocky.

1050
00:33:13,125 --> 00:33:14,227
And because of this--

1051
00:33:14,260 --> 00:33:15,327
-I'm Eleanor Roosevelt!

1052
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:17,297
- --it can be far
more dangerous.

1053
00:33:17,330 --> 00:33:19,065
-Oh, I see what you
mean, Professor Newton.

1054
00:33:19,098 --> 00:33:20,065
-Twisted old fruit.

1055
00:33:20,098 --> 00:33:22,235
-While the Gypsy Moons
themselves aren't large,

1056
00:33:22,268 --> 00:33:23,770
the orbit they describe is.

1057
00:33:23,803 --> 00:33:26,072
-Like children of a playground.

1058
00:33:26,105 --> 00:33:27,005
-Uh, now, look, honey.

1059
00:33:27,038 --> 00:33:28,340
Why do you just go
make some sandwiches?

1060
00:33:28,373 --> 00:33:28,907
OK?

1061
00:33:28,940 --> 00:33:29,708
-Here, let me show you.

1062
00:33:29,742 --> 00:33:31,143
Bobby.

1063
00:33:31,177 --> 00:33:32,245
The way they move
through space--

1064
00:33:32,278 --> 00:33:33,412
-OK, hit it, Joe.

1065
00:33:33,445 --> 00:33:35,380
- --it's something like two
children on a playground.

1066
00:33:35,413 --> 00:33:37,417
Bobby is Posita and
I'm the other moon,

1067
00:33:37,450 --> 00:33:40,620
Nagato Our arms and hands
are the atmosphere chain.

1068
00:33:40,653 --> 00:33:43,222
They move through space
spinning around each other.

1069
00:33:43,255 --> 00:33:44,288
-Yeah, yeah.

1070
00:33:44,322 --> 00:33:45,525
And I guess the moons sing
"Ring Around the Rosie!"

1071
00:33:45,558 --> 00:33:46,192
Get out!

1072
00:33:46,225 --> 00:33:47,560
Get out!

1073
00:33:47,593 --> 00:33:52,132
-But if I spin myself, I
don't cover half as much area.

1074
00:33:52,165 --> 00:33:54,667
-So what would happen if one
moon sat down and shut up?

1075
00:33:54,700 --> 00:33:55,367
-Now--

1076
00:33:55,400 --> 00:33:56,502
-Back to work.

1077
00:33:56,535 --> 00:33:58,270
- --this is my great
concern, Rocky.

1078
00:33:58,303 --> 00:33:59,572
-Where are my gummy bears?

1079
00:33:59,605 --> 00:34:02,708
-Magnify this by tens
of thousands of miles,

1080
00:34:02,742 --> 00:34:05,578
and you see-- you see
what tremendous danger

1081
00:34:05,612 --> 00:34:06,745
we're confronted with.

1082
00:34:06,778 --> 00:34:08,380
-Uh, Vladimer, if you get
to an issue that's relevant,

1083
00:34:08,413 --> 00:34:09,180
let us know.

1084
00:34:09,213 --> 00:34:11,350
-For example, say
there's a planet

1085
00:34:11,383 --> 00:34:13,652
or a moon right over there.

1086
00:34:13,685 --> 00:34:14,218
-OK.

1087
00:34:14,252 --> 00:34:18,290
-Bobby, go ahead again.

1088
00:34:18,323 --> 00:34:19,292
-It's on my birthday!

1089
00:34:19,325 --> 00:34:20,392
-Mr. Secretary!

1090
00:34:20,425 --> 00:34:21,693
I'm sorry.

1091
00:34:21,727 --> 00:34:23,162
-What's going on?

1092
00:34:23,195 --> 00:34:24,162
-She blinded me with science!

1093
00:34:24,195 --> 00:34:26,665
-An illustration of an
astronomical phenomenon,

1094
00:34:26,698 --> 00:34:27,732
Mr. Secretary.

1095
00:34:27,765 --> 00:34:31,770
-Yeah, it, uh, it seems
that you are a planet, Mr.

1096
00:34:31,803 --> 00:34:34,173
Secretary, and Vena is Posita--

1097
00:34:34,207 --> 00:34:34,707
-Hm?

1098
00:34:34,740 --> 00:34:36,242
-And Bobby's Nagato.

1099
00:34:36,275 --> 00:34:36,842
-Hm?

1100
00:34:36,875 --> 00:34:38,210
-No, no, no.

1101
00:34:38,243 --> 00:34:40,747
Bobby is Posita
and Vena is Nagato.

1102
00:34:40,780 --> 00:34:41,880
-In-A-Gadda-Da-Vida, baby!

1103
00:34:41,913 --> 00:34:44,550
-You-- you could really
either be a planet or a moon,

1104
00:34:44,583 --> 00:34:46,385
but as it happens,
you're planet.

1105
00:34:46,418 --> 00:34:49,322
So you see what happens?

1106
00:34:49,355 --> 00:34:50,322
-I uh--

1107
00:34:50,355 --> 00:34:51,890
-Bob Saget, ladies and
gentlemen, Bob Saget.

1108
00:35:00,398 --> 00:35:02,735
-Orbit Jet to
Posita headquarters.

1109
00:35:02,768 --> 00:35:03,870
-The baby's talking!

1110
00:35:03,903 --> 00:35:05,772
-Bavarro, come in, Bavarro.

1111
00:35:05,805 --> 00:35:06,838
-Infant one to mother!

1112
00:35:06,872 --> 00:35:08,407
-Come in, Bavarro.

1113
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:08,840
-Bavarro!

1114
00:35:08,873 --> 00:35:11,643
Come Bavarro.

1115
00:35:11,677 --> 00:35:12,845
-What, Potonda?

1116
00:35:12,878 --> 00:35:14,747
We were going to speak
they're language?

1117
00:35:14,780 --> 00:35:15,882
-(WITH GERMAN
ACCENT) Say nothing.

1118
00:35:15,915 --> 00:35:17,683
-It is Squawky Jones.

1119
00:35:17,717 --> 00:35:18,783
-Squawky Jones?

1120
00:35:18,817 --> 00:35:20,352
-Now that's rude.

1121
00:35:20,385 --> 00:35:21,653
Come down Bavarro.

1122
00:35:21,687 --> 00:35:22,153
Talk to him.

1123
00:35:22,187 --> 00:35:24,423
-I married a Nazi.

1124
00:35:24,457 --> 00:35:26,492
-Orbit Jet to--

1125
00:35:26,525 --> 00:35:27,427
-Rocky Jones!

1126
00:35:27,460 --> 00:35:29,628
-My thumb is swollen and purple.

1127
00:35:29,662 --> 00:35:31,997
-We've tried to
vex one language.

1128
00:35:32,030 --> 00:35:33,365
-My neighbor chatza.

1129
00:35:33,398 --> 00:35:34,700
-Ah, her hair changed sides.

1130
00:35:34,733 --> 00:35:35,700
Did you see that?

1131
00:35:35,733 --> 00:35:38,603
-Professor Newton, and--
and Bobby, and Winky.

1132
00:35:38,637 --> 00:35:39,972
-And Poco and poopie
pants, and greasy Dan.

1133
00:35:40,005 --> 00:35:43,575
-This is Dinky, uh, Winky--
she's got me doing it.

1134
00:35:43,608 --> 00:35:46,545
Bobby and the Professor are
with us, and so is Vena.

1135
00:35:46,578 --> 00:35:47,680
-Bavarro.

1136
00:35:47,713 --> 00:35:48,915
-Yes, Rocky.

1137
00:35:48,948 --> 00:35:50,650
-We're in the
ellipse of your moon.

1138
00:35:50,683 --> 00:35:53,018
Landing time, 0214.

1139
00:35:53,052 --> 00:35:54,520
-Hurry in, Rocky.

1140
00:35:54,553 --> 00:35:56,355
This is so-- so clandindo.

1141
00:35:56,388 --> 00:35:58,090
Uh, clandindo--

1142
00:35:58,123 --> 00:35:58,957
-The sap!

1143
00:35:58,990 --> 00:36:01,827
Thinks he's on "Hogan's
Heroes" already.

1144
00:36:01,860 --> 00:36:03,462
-Oop, I can't take a crap.

1145
00:36:03,495 --> 00:36:04,897
Bobby's my witness.

1146
00:36:04,930 --> 00:36:05,732
-He's right.

1147
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:11,370
-Oh, they're landing on
the planet of Magic Rocks.

1148
00:36:11,403 --> 00:36:11,803
-Ew.

1149
00:36:18,777 --> 00:36:22,582
-Welcome, to our cardboard home.

1150
00:36:22,615 --> 00:36:23,148
-By Vena!

1151
00:36:23,182 --> 00:36:25,117
Have fun at German camp!

1152
00:36:25,150 --> 00:36:27,185
-Contombo!

1153
00:36:27,218 --> 00:36:28,820
Contombo, Rocky!

1154
00:36:28,853 --> 00:36:29,687
-Is that Swahili?

1155
00:36:29,720 --> 00:36:31,990
-I have such wonderful
news to share.

1156
00:36:32,023 --> 00:36:33,458
-Zorro painted mine house!

1157
00:36:33,492 --> 00:36:35,127
-You see how happy we--

1158
00:36:35,160 --> 00:36:36,728
-Horowitz is getting smaller.

1159
00:36:36,762 --> 00:36:37,695
-I know.

1160
00:36:37,728 --> 00:36:40,800
-I just couldn't bring
myself to tell her.

1161
00:36:40,833 --> 00:36:43,135
-Can there be a
mistake, Professor?

1162
00:36:43,168 --> 00:36:46,872
Is the collision between
Ophecius and Posita inevitable?

1163
00:36:46,905 --> 00:36:49,575
-I double-checked
my equations, Rocky.

1164
00:36:49,608 --> 00:36:51,610
-Yeah, ya double-checked
'em last time, too.

1165
00:36:51,643 --> 00:36:53,947
- --the slightest
margin for error.

1166
00:36:53,980 --> 00:36:56,015
-Ophecius, Cleolanta's
planet, which

1167
00:36:56,048 --> 00:36:57,115
didn't need any
help from anyone.

1168
00:36:57,148 --> 00:36:59,618
-Men, just ignore him.

1169
00:36:59,652 --> 00:37:01,687
-She'll need plenty, now.

1170
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:03,222
A fleet of spaceships
for evacuation.

1171
00:37:03,255 --> 00:37:04,223
-Shut up, Winky.

1172
00:37:04,257 --> 00:37:05,290
Just shut up!

1173
00:37:05,323 --> 00:37:07,927
-Bavarro, to him, his
moon is a place of beauty.

1174
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:10,128
His whole world.

1175
00:37:10,162 --> 00:37:10,695
-Sit down!

1176
00:37:10,728 --> 00:37:11,863
-Well, we'd better go.

1177
00:37:11,897 --> 00:37:14,833
He has to be told.

1178
00:37:14,867 --> 00:37:16,735
-Now he can be told!

1179
00:37:16,768 --> 00:37:17,937
-Uh, is someone gonna drive?

1180
00:37:17,970 --> 00:37:19,505
Uh, wait for me.

1181
00:37:19,538 --> 00:37:21,540
-Oh, Potonda, he's beautiful.

1182
00:37:21,573 --> 00:37:22,542
-I'll take him.

1183
00:37:22,575 --> 00:37:23,942
-Beautiful?

1184
00:37:23,975 --> 00:37:24,843
What is that, you say?

1185
00:37:24,877 --> 00:37:26,212
His mother is beautiful.

1186
00:37:26,245 --> 00:37:27,680
My son is strong.

1187
00:37:27,713 --> 00:37:28,280
[CHUCKLING]

1188
00:37:28,313 --> 00:37:29,815
-All right, then.

1189
00:37:29,848 --> 00:37:32,183
He's beautiful and strong.

1190
00:37:32,217 --> 00:37:33,417
-Good.

1191
00:37:33,450 --> 00:37:36,822
The next ruler of Posita, he
will be beautiful and strong!

1192
00:37:36,855 --> 00:37:38,190
-Of za purest race!

1193
00:37:38,223 --> 00:37:39,258
[BELL SOUNDING]

1194
00:37:39,292 --> 00:37:40,760
-If you'd like to make a call.

1195
00:37:40,793 --> 00:37:41,627
-Wait here!

1196
00:37:41,660 --> 00:37:43,862
I wish to surprise
Rocky with my son.

1197
00:37:43,895 --> 00:37:45,563
-He's gonna give Rocky his son?

1198
00:37:45,597 --> 00:37:47,132
[THUNDER]

1199
00:37:47,165 --> 00:37:49,035
-This gets him every time.

1200
00:37:49,068 --> 00:37:51,637
This is going to be a doozie!

1201
00:37:51,670 --> 00:37:52,270
-Rocky Jones!

1202
00:37:52,303 --> 00:37:53,272
-Hello, Bavarro.

1203
00:37:53,305 --> 00:37:55,708
-Welcome to Posita.

1204
00:37:55,742 --> 00:37:56,708
Bobby!

1205
00:37:56,742 --> 00:37:57,542
-Poopie?

1206
00:37:57,575 --> 00:37:58,677
-Why was I not
lucky enough to have

1207
00:37:58,710 --> 00:38:02,147
a son who would grow up to
be a fine boy like Bobby?

1208
00:38:02,180 --> 00:38:04,017
Welcome to Posita, Bobby.

1209
00:38:04,050 --> 00:38:04,417
-Ah, you smell.

1210
00:38:04,450 --> 00:38:05,450
-Welcome.

1211
00:38:05,483 --> 00:38:07,887
Then he could be a brave
man, like Rocky Jones.

1212
00:38:07,920 --> 00:38:08,887
-Uh, who the hell are you?

1213
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:10,823
-Oh, Bavarro, I want you
to meet Secretary Drake.

1214
00:38:10,857 --> 00:38:12,057
-Bavarro.

1215
00:38:12,090 --> 00:38:14,860
-Or my son could be a great
leader, like Secretary Drake.

1216
00:38:14,893 --> 00:38:16,662
I heard so much about
you, Mr. Secretary.

1217
00:38:16,695 --> 00:38:17,362
Welcome to Posita.

1218
00:38:17,395 --> 00:38:18,363
-Man, they're dopple-gangers.

1219
00:38:18,397 --> 00:38:19,297
Look at 'em.

1220
00:38:19,330 --> 00:38:21,367
-Or my son could have
a brilliant mind,

1221
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:23,235
like Professor Newton, here.

1222
00:38:23,268 --> 00:38:24,403
Welcome, Professor.

1223
00:38:24,437 --> 00:38:26,072
-Bavarro, you honor me.

1224
00:38:26,105 --> 00:38:27,940
-Bavarro, and
Bavano, and Bavarro.

1225
00:38:27,973 --> 00:38:28,973
Kliepsen.

1226
00:38:29,007 --> 00:38:29,842
-Hi, Bavarro.

1227
00:38:29,875 --> 00:38:30,743
-Oh, Hi, Winky.

1228
00:38:30,777 --> 00:38:31,177
-Winky!

1229
00:38:33,978 --> 00:38:36,415
Or like Winky, my
son would, um--

1230
00:38:36,448 --> 00:38:38,750
-Would get beat up
in the third grade.

1231
00:38:38,783 --> 00:38:41,920
-Would have a huge heart, and a
wonderful twinkle in his eyes.

1232
00:38:41,953 --> 00:38:43,288
Gentlemen.

1233
00:38:43,322 --> 00:38:45,758
I was afraid we'll
never meet again, Rocky.

1234
00:38:45,792 --> 00:38:48,260
My moon travels a
lot, Mr. Secretary.

1235
00:38:48,293 --> 00:38:48,993
-Yes.

1236
00:38:49,027 --> 00:38:50,763
-You're a lonely
man, aren't you?

1237
00:38:50,797 --> 00:38:52,130
-We've been targeting
your course.

1238
00:38:52,163 --> 00:38:53,130
-Mel Torme!

1239
00:38:53,163 --> 00:38:57,268
-The way the Gypsy
Moons, Posita and Nagato,

1240
00:38:57,302 --> 00:39:04,077
travel through space, it's
an astronomical phenomenon!

1241
00:39:04,110 --> 00:39:05,010
-Pig Face!

1242
00:39:05,043 --> 00:39:06,178
-Ha, ha, ha.

1243
00:39:06,212 --> 00:39:08,113
What is phenom--

1244
00:39:08,147 --> 00:39:09,782
-Something unusual, Bavarro.

1245
00:39:09,815 --> 00:39:10,615
-Something that happens.

1246
00:39:10,648 --> 00:39:12,418
-You see the
atmosphere which joins

1247
00:39:12,452 --> 00:39:14,453
the two moons serves as a chain.

1248
00:39:14,487 --> 00:39:15,420
-Uh-huh?

1249
00:39:15,453 --> 00:39:18,090
-One moon swings the
other, then the other--

1250
00:39:18,123 --> 00:39:20,458
-And I swing both ways.

1251
00:39:20,492 --> 00:39:25,030
-Strange that we don't
get, uh, uh, dizzy, huh?

1252
00:39:25,063 --> 00:39:27,032
-Bavarro, please,
listen carefully.

1253
00:39:27,065 --> 00:39:27,933
-You're fired.

1254
00:39:27,967 --> 00:39:29,502
-On the 19th of next month--

1255
00:39:29,535 --> 00:39:30,435
-Where were you?

1256
00:39:30,468 --> 00:39:34,940
- --your moon, Posita
will-- will crash,

1257
00:39:34,973 --> 00:39:36,208
head on, into Ophecius.

1258
00:39:36,242 --> 00:39:38,010
-Hm?

1259
00:39:38,043 --> 00:39:38,877
-Both will be destroyed.

1260
00:39:38,910 --> 00:39:39,912
-Just do London Bridges.

1261
00:39:39,945 --> 00:39:40,880
Show him how it works.

1262
00:39:40,913 --> 00:39:42,180
-What?

1263
00:39:42,213 --> 00:39:45,050
What are you saying?

1264
00:39:45,083 --> 00:39:46,585
Posita is going to be destroyed?

1265
00:39:46,618 --> 00:39:48,087
-Unless you buy
these magazines, now.

1266
00:39:48,120 --> 00:39:50,155
-Yes, Bavarro.

1267
00:39:50,188 --> 00:39:51,157
-No.

1268
00:39:51,190 --> 00:39:52,492
-Oh, he's pleased to know it.

1269
00:39:52,525 --> 00:39:54,460
-It will not happen.

1270
00:39:54,493 --> 00:39:56,028
Never!

1271
00:39:56,062 --> 00:39:57,128
I will not let it happen!

1272
00:39:57,162 --> 00:39:57,695
Never!

1273
00:39:57,728 --> 00:39:58,530
-OK, we're convinced.

1274
00:39:58,563 --> 00:39:59,397
Fine!

1275
00:39:59,430 --> 00:40:02,167
-Now, now, little
prince, don't cry.

1276
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:03,035
-Oh, honey!

1277
00:40:03,068 --> 00:40:04,268
-Ooh!

1278
00:40:04,302 --> 00:40:05,403
[IMITATING POPEYE) Sweet Pea's
trying to tell us somethun.

1279
00:40:07,607 --> 00:40:11,377
-You know, Vena, in
some strange way,

1280
00:40:11,410 --> 00:40:14,947
our baby knew about Posita's
tragedy before Rocky told us.

1281
00:40:14,980 --> 00:40:18,250
-Oh sure, everybody's
baby is so smart.

1282
00:40:18,283 --> 00:40:21,587
-I have had great
pride in Posita.

1283
00:40:21,620 --> 00:40:24,423
More than anything, I'm
distressed that my son

1284
00:40:24,457 --> 00:40:26,892
shall lose his heritage.

1285
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:27,825
-Coo-coo!

1286
00:40:27,858 --> 00:40:30,495
-How the people of
Ophecius must hate us.

1287
00:40:30,528 --> 00:40:33,565
Their moon stands
still in all innocence,

1288
00:40:33,598 --> 00:40:35,533
while we rush forward
to destroy it.

1289
00:40:35,567 --> 00:40:37,970
-Got kind of a Spritz cookie
cutter on his chest, there.

1290
00:40:38,003 --> 00:40:39,172
-Have they started
the evacuation?

1291
00:40:39,205 --> 00:40:39,605
-Evac?

1292
00:40:39,638 --> 00:40:41,373
Oh, evacuation.

1293
00:40:41,407 --> 00:40:43,442
-They don't know
what's going to happen.

1294
00:40:43,475 --> 00:40:47,078
-Ophecius is ruled by an
arrogant woman named Cleolanta.

1295
00:40:47,112 --> 00:40:49,482
She won't allow her people
any information about life

1296
00:40:49,515 --> 00:40:51,417
on other moons and planets.

1297
00:40:51,450 --> 00:40:53,218
-Even the possession
of an astrophone set

1298
00:40:53,252 --> 00:40:55,187
is punishable by death.

1299
00:40:55,220 --> 00:40:56,988
We tried to reason
with Cleolanta, but--

1300
00:40:57,022 --> 00:40:58,323
-And we secretly switched her--

1301
00:40:58,357 --> 00:41:01,060
-She even threatened to
kill us, if we returned.

1302
00:41:01,093 --> 00:41:02,227
-But she must know.

1303
00:41:02,260 --> 00:41:03,595
She must be warned.

1304
00:41:03,628 --> 00:41:05,197
-She will be.

1305
00:41:05,230 --> 00:41:08,433
Mr. Secretary, may I suggest
you go with Bavarro to Nagato,

1306
00:41:08,467 --> 00:41:10,702
and meet with Torvak, the ruler?

1307
00:41:10,735 --> 00:41:12,370
We'll need his help
in the evacuation.

1308
00:41:12,403 --> 00:41:13,972
-Oh, yeah, I'll take
orders from you.

1309
00:41:14,005 --> 00:41:14,973
-Professor Newton--

1310
00:41:15,007 --> 00:41:16,240
-You make cookies.

1311
00:41:16,273 --> 00:41:17,977
-You and Vena and Bobby will do
what you can, here on Posita,

1312
00:41:18,010 --> 00:41:19,645
while Winky and I are gone.

1313
00:41:19,678 --> 00:41:22,013
There must not be any
panic among the people.

1314
00:41:22,047 --> 00:41:23,515
-Yes, Rocky.

1315
00:41:23,548 --> 00:41:26,752
-Mr. Secretary, we'll leave
for Ophecius immediately.

1316
00:41:26,785 --> 00:41:30,055
-Hey Rocky, couldn't we rig
up a space anchor for Posita?

1317
00:41:30,088 --> 00:41:32,357
-No, we're not gonna
rig up a space anchor!

1318
00:41:32,390 --> 00:41:33,692
-If we only could, Bobby.

1319
00:41:33,725 --> 00:41:35,127
That would be a great solution.

1320
00:41:37,562 --> 00:41:38,130
[THUNDER]

1321
00:41:38,163 --> 00:41:38,663
-Ha!

1322
00:41:38,697 --> 00:41:39,332
I love that pooper.

1323
00:41:44,770 --> 00:41:48,440
-When in the Ukraine,
visit Chernobyl.

1324
00:41:48,473 --> 00:41:52,343
-So, um, who's leaving, here?

1325
00:41:52,377 --> 00:41:53,312
-Uh?

1326
00:41:53,345 --> 00:41:55,213
-Uh, we don't--

1327
00:41:55,247 --> 00:41:57,448
-Looks like the land of
Dairy Queen gone wrong.

1328
00:42:01,887 --> 00:42:02,788
-But you can't marry Ken.

1329
00:42:02,822 --> 00:42:03,722
You don't love him.

1330
00:42:07,793 --> 00:42:10,362
-Trinka?

1331
00:42:10,395 --> 00:42:11,563
-Jump on.

1332
00:42:11,597 --> 00:42:13,298
-Well, aren't you proud of me?

1333
00:42:13,332 --> 00:42:15,767
Today, I have a special
audience to Cleolanta.

1334
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:18,470
My, uh, Suzerain says she has
great plans in store for me.

1335
00:42:18,503 --> 00:42:20,772
-So why are you dressed
as Liberace's chauffeur?

1336
00:42:20,805 --> 00:42:22,642
-Well, aren't you proud of me?

1337
00:42:22,675 --> 00:42:24,577
-We used to have
plans, too, Atlasan.

1338
00:42:24,610 --> 00:42:25,843
-Hm.

1339
00:42:25,877 --> 00:42:27,813
-We were going to leave Ophecius
and see how other people lived.

1340
00:42:27,847 --> 00:42:29,682
-To me, Ophecius comes first.

1341
00:42:29,715 --> 00:42:31,917
You're talking as foolishly
as a child, Trinka.

1342
00:42:31,950 --> 00:42:33,318
-Yes, sir.

1343
00:42:33,352 --> 00:42:34,487
-And that's, uh, pretty foolish.

1344
00:42:34,520 --> 00:42:35,520
It's my point.

1345
00:42:38,423 --> 00:42:39,392
-Jeez!

1346
00:42:39,425 --> 00:42:42,662
And the women who love them!

1347
00:42:42,695 --> 00:42:46,665
-Glad she's dressed
for her Rumplemintz ad.

1348
00:42:46,698 --> 00:42:48,933
-I better hit the bottle.

1349
00:42:48,967 --> 00:42:50,735
-Even in the future,
booze satisfies.

1350
00:42:55,407 --> 00:42:55,807
-Hey!

1351
00:42:59,545 --> 00:43:00,812
-Breaker, breaker, good buddy.

1352
00:43:00,845 --> 00:43:03,815
This is the Hot Pagoda.

1353
00:43:03,848 --> 00:43:06,185
-Pigs in space!

1354
00:43:08,620 --> 00:43:12,390
-So, ya ever think you'd be just
sitting here saying nothing?

1355
00:43:12,423 --> 00:43:13,925
-Well, there's Ophecius.

1356
00:43:13,958 --> 00:43:16,295
-This is your scalp
before treatment, Winky.

1357
00:43:16,328 --> 00:43:17,362
-Cut rockets, Winky.

1358
00:43:17,395 --> 00:43:18,997
We'll stand off and try
to get a message through.

1359
00:43:19,030 --> 00:43:22,333
-Uh, take a left here, and
we'll try to parallel park.

1360
00:43:22,367 --> 00:43:24,570
-We'll be lucky if we can
get through to Ophecius.

1361
00:43:24,603 --> 00:43:26,505
Cleolanta always jams
and garbles our messages.

1362
00:43:26,538 --> 00:43:27,072
[GARBLED MUMBLING]

1363
00:43:27,105 --> 00:43:28,038
-You're right, Winky.

1364
00:43:28,072 --> 00:43:28,840
I know we can't get
through to Cleolanta,

1365
00:43:28,873 --> 00:43:31,510
but we'll try for
the underground.

1366
00:43:31,543 --> 00:43:33,345
You see, there's an
underground faction there,

1367
00:43:33,378 --> 00:43:35,613
in favor of joining
the United Worlds.

1368
00:43:35,647 --> 00:43:37,750
If they have a secret
astrophone set,

1369
00:43:37,783 --> 00:43:39,518
they can relay my
message to Cleolanta.

1370
00:43:39,552 --> 00:43:41,587
-You know, Rocky's got
all of facial expressions

1371
00:43:41,620 --> 00:43:42,788
of Troy Tempest.

1372
00:43:42,822 --> 00:43:43,222
-This is--

1373
00:43:43,255 --> 00:43:44,188
-That's right.

1374
00:43:44,222 --> 00:43:45,490
- --Rocky Jones in the
Space Ranger's ship,

1375
00:43:45,523 --> 00:43:48,360
Orbit Jet to Ophecius.

1376
00:43:48,393 --> 00:43:49,628
-Rocky Jones!

1377
00:43:49,662 --> 00:43:50,362
-Cybil Faulty.

1378
00:43:50,395 --> 00:43:51,830
-Alert Ophecius.

1379
00:43:51,863 --> 00:43:52,230
Alert.

1380
00:43:52,263 --> 00:43:52,930
Learn this.

1381
00:43:52,963 --> 00:43:53,732
-Ya, well, learn this, Rocky.

1382
00:43:53,765 --> 00:43:55,700
-The moons, Posita
and Nagato are

1383
00:43:55,733 --> 00:43:57,970
traveling in our solar system.

1384
00:43:58,003 --> 00:43:58,837
On the 19th--

1385
00:43:58,870 --> 00:43:59,470
-Uh-huh.

1386
00:43:59,503 --> 00:44:00,170
- --the moon Posita will--

1387
00:44:00,203 --> 00:44:01,773
-(IMITATING STEWIE) Oh, I know.

1388
00:44:01,807 --> 00:44:02,473
I know!

1389
00:44:02,507 --> 00:44:05,477
-Cleolanta must be told at once!

1390
00:44:05,510 --> 00:44:08,413
An evacuation must be planned.

1391
00:44:08,447 --> 00:44:10,282
United World's offer
all possible assistance.

1392
00:44:16,622 --> 00:44:19,123
-We all remember John
Banner, Sergeant Schultz

1393
00:44:19,157 --> 00:44:21,460
from TVs "Hogan's
Heroes," the sitcom

1394
00:44:21,493 --> 00:44:23,995
that pokes fun at wartime
atrocities in such

1395
00:44:24,028 --> 00:44:25,730
a life-affirming way.

1396
00:44:25,763 --> 00:44:26,732
Yes, yes.

1397
00:44:26,765 --> 00:44:27,965
John Banner.

1398
00:44:27,998 --> 00:44:30,135
Probably the most affable man
that ever walked this earth.

1399
00:44:30,168 --> 00:44:32,403
And now, with the
Bannergram, you

1400
00:44:32,437 --> 00:44:34,840
can send John Banner
and his warm greetings

1401
00:44:34,873 --> 00:44:37,743
anywhere-- across the
street or across the nation.

1402
00:44:37,777 --> 00:44:40,678
-Yes John Banner, like
Pope John the 23rd,

1403
00:44:40,712 --> 00:44:42,147
gathering little children
unto his bosom, he--

1404
00:44:42,180 --> 00:44:44,148
-Oh, better than
Pope John the 23rd.

1405
00:44:44,182 --> 00:44:45,083
-Uh, you're right.

1406
00:44:45,117 --> 00:44:45,783
Much better.

1407
00:44:45,817 --> 00:44:47,787
So cheer up Aunt Jean in Denver.

1408
00:44:47,820 --> 00:44:51,157
-Or congratulate Cousin Bob,
for no reason at all, in Denver.

1409
00:44:51,190 --> 00:44:54,760
-Or just send John Banner
to yourself, in Denver.

1410
00:44:54,793 --> 00:44:57,028
Believe me, you'll feel
warm and wonderful.

1411
00:44:57,062 --> 00:44:58,797
Just pick up the phone and say--

1412
00:44:58,830 --> 00:45:00,065
-I want to send a Bannergram.

1413
00:45:00,098 --> 00:45:01,667
-A few quick keystrokes, and--

1414
00:45:01,700 --> 00:45:02,300
-Ha, ha, ha!

1415
00:45:02,333 --> 00:45:03,768
-John Banner for everyone!

1416
00:45:03,802 --> 00:45:04,968
Love and happiness.

1417
00:45:05,002 --> 00:45:07,105
-Hey, I, uh, Joel, I bet that's
fun to send a Bannergram.

1418
00:45:07,138 --> 00:45:07,472
-Um, hm.

1419
00:45:07,505 --> 00:45:07,905
Go ahead.

1420
00:45:07,938 --> 00:45:08,172
-Uh, let me try.

1421
00:45:08,205 --> 00:45:08,973
Uh--

1422
00:45:09,007 --> 00:45:10,040
-Oh, no.

1423
00:45:10,073 --> 00:45:12,443
-Uh, I did it wrong, I
sent a John Boehner-gram.

1424
00:45:12,477 --> 00:45:13,343
That's great.

1425
00:45:13,377 --> 00:45:14,212
-And I just sent a
David Brenner-gram.

1426
00:45:14,245 --> 00:45:14,813
-Oh, no.

1427
00:45:14,847 --> 00:45:15,613
-Look out!

1428
00:45:15,647 --> 00:45:17,515
-Wait, I sent a
Lucas Tanner-gram.

1429
00:45:17,548 --> 00:45:18,650
-A Lou Gosset Jr-gram.

1430
00:45:18,683 --> 00:45:19,585
Hoo-hoo.

1431
00:45:19,618 --> 00:45:20,718
-A Junior Samples-gram.

1432
00:45:20,752 --> 00:45:22,788
-A Whitman Sampler-gram.

1433
00:45:22,822 --> 00:45:23,788
Oh, no.

1434
00:45:23,822 --> 00:45:25,557
Now you've got me doing
it, you little devils.

1435
00:45:25,590 --> 00:45:26,657
-Ah!

1436
00:45:26,690 --> 00:45:28,593
-But it's all a good example
of the wholesome effect

1437
00:45:28,627 --> 00:45:31,930
John Banner brings to any
family or social event.

1438
00:45:31,963 --> 00:45:35,633
Spontaneous fun, good-hearted
enjoyment, likes you best.

1439
00:45:35,667 --> 00:45:37,102
-I love John Banner!

1440
00:45:37,135 --> 00:45:38,870
-Because he loves me.

1441
00:45:38,903 --> 00:45:39,370
-Hm.

1442
00:45:39,403 --> 00:45:40,303
-Here's one more.

1443
00:45:40,337 --> 00:45:43,608
-Oh no, you sent a
David Mammogram, Crow!

1444
00:45:43,642 --> 00:45:44,275
-I know nothing!

1445
00:45:44,308 --> 00:45:45,043
Nothing!

1446
00:45:45,077 --> 00:45:45,543
-Look out!

1447
00:45:45,577 --> 00:45:46,578
We got movie-gram!

1448
00:45:58,290 --> 00:45:58,923
-Huh!

1449
00:45:58,957 --> 00:46:00,192
A wife, Blythe Danner-gram.

1450
00:46:00,225 --> 00:46:00,858
-Ha, ha, ha.

1451
00:46:00,892 --> 00:46:02,227
I think that's a great one.

1452
00:46:02,260 --> 00:46:03,160
-Well, that was a bust.

1453
00:46:03,193 --> 00:46:04,362
I was parading down
the hall in my sash,

1454
00:46:04,395 --> 00:46:06,832
and the award ceremony doesn't
even start till next week.

1455
00:46:06,865 --> 00:46:08,267
Trinka, will you forgive me?

1456
00:46:08,300 --> 00:46:09,602
-Of course, I will,
Thunder Thighs.

1457
00:46:09,635 --> 00:46:11,903
-As you know, I-- I'm ambitious.

1458
00:46:11,937 --> 00:46:13,272
And I love Ophecius.

1459
00:46:13,305 --> 00:46:14,338
-And I'm not superstitious.

1460
00:46:14,372 --> 00:46:14,972
And you look delicious.

1461
00:46:15,005 --> 00:46:16,942
-I also love you, Trinka.

1462
00:46:16,975 --> 00:46:17,942
-Hey!

1463
00:46:17,975 --> 00:46:21,947
-Which is the greater
love, uh, I don't know.

1464
00:46:21,980 --> 00:46:22,747
-Atlasan--

1465
00:46:22,780 --> 00:46:23,313
It's a paint-by-number
Kandinsky,

1466
00:46:23,347 --> 00:46:24,282
up there on the wall.

1467
00:46:24,315 --> 00:46:25,883
-United Worlds offer
all possible assistance.

1468
00:46:25,917 --> 00:46:26,785
-Huh?

1469
00:46:26,818 --> 00:46:27,752
-I'll repeat the message.

1470
00:46:27,785 --> 00:46:29,622
-You're wearing a wire,
aren't ya, darling?

1471
00:46:29,655 --> 00:46:30,322
-United Worlds?

1472
00:46:30,355 --> 00:46:31,223
-I love that show.

1473
00:46:34,158 --> 00:46:35,360
-Trinka?

1474
00:46:35,393 --> 00:46:37,395
-Atlasan, please,
please forgive me.

1475
00:46:37,428 --> 00:46:40,098
But you must listen to
what the voice is saying.

1476
00:46:40,132 --> 00:46:41,867
-Hm?

1477
00:46:41,900 --> 00:46:44,035
-Now it's garbage!

1478
00:46:44,068 --> 00:46:46,738
-Uh-oh!

1479
00:46:46,772 --> 00:46:52,143
-This is Rocky Jones in the
Orbit Jet, clear to Ophecius.

1480
00:46:52,177 --> 00:46:53,077
-Oh, boy.

1481
00:46:53,110 --> 00:46:54,813
-Well, I guess I'm
not here, huh, Rocky?

1482
00:46:54,847 --> 00:46:57,315
-Think we got through, Rocky?

1483
00:46:57,348 --> 00:46:58,483
-I doubt it, Winky.

1484
00:46:58,517 --> 00:47:01,720
If Cleolanta heard our
message, there'd be some reply.

1485
00:47:01,753 --> 00:47:04,823
A warning to stay clear,
because she didn't believe us.

1486
00:47:04,857 --> 00:47:07,125
Or a demand that we
prove our information.

1487
00:47:07,158 --> 00:47:07,893
-Hm.

1488
00:47:07,927 --> 00:47:08,827
-So?

1489
00:47:08,860 --> 00:47:09,995
-Oh, I don't know, Winky.

1490
00:47:10,028 --> 00:47:10,562
-Rockets on, Winky.

1491
00:47:10,595 --> 00:47:11,930
We'll attempt a landing.

1492
00:47:11,963 --> 00:47:12,932
-Aye, aye, sir.

1493
00:47:18,337 --> 00:47:19,805
-Huh.

1494
00:47:19,838 --> 00:47:21,407
-You know, it doesn't
feel like a Thursday.

1495
00:47:21,440 --> 00:47:22,273
-Hm, mm.

1496
00:47:22,307 --> 00:47:24,743
Hm.

1497
00:47:24,777 --> 00:47:28,247
-My first lobotomy kit, by Sony.

1498
00:47:28,280 --> 00:47:31,850
-Who else is in this underground
conspiracy against us?

1499
00:47:31,883 --> 00:47:33,085
-Oh, just Betty next door.

1500
00:47:33,118 --> 00:47:35,453
-I'm not in any conspiracy
against Ophecius.

1501
00:47:35,487 --> 00:47:37,957
But you must listen to me.

1502
00:47:37,990 --> 00:47:38,923
-You'll answer my questions--

1503
00:47:38,957 --> 00:47:39,457
-Mm.

1504
00:47:39,490 --> 00:47:40,390
- --and that is all.

1505
00:47:40,423 --> 00:47:41,092
-Can I flick that thing
off your forehead?

1506
00:47:41,125 --> 00:47:43,962
-Who else is in the conspiracy?

1507
00:47:43,995 --> 00:47:44,962
-No one.

1508
00:47:44,995 --> 00:47:46,832
I only wanted to hear
how other people lived

1509
00:47:46,865 --> 00:47:48,167
and what they were like.

1510
00:47:48,200 --> 00:47:50,302
And I love Ophecius
as much as you.

1511
00:47:50,335 --> 00:47:51,537
-You answer my
Suzerain's questions,

1512
00:47:51,570 --> 00:47:53,072
and not one more word!

1513
00:47:53,105 --> 00:47:54,172
-That turns me on.

1514
00:47:54,205 --> 00:47:56,408
-That's very good, Atlasan.

1515
00:47:56,442 --> 00:47:57,977
Knowing the
punishment, it wasn't

1516
00:47:58,010 --> 00:48:00,545
easy to report your
wife's betrayal.

1517
00:48:00,578 --> 00:48:01,245
-Thank you, Cleolanta.

1518
00:48:01,278 --> 00:48:02,380
-I'm still mad at you, though.

1519
00:48:02,413 --> 00:48:04,883
-Cleolanta, my Suzerain.

1520
00:48:04,917 --> 00:48:05,350
-Yes?

1521
00:48:05,383 --> 00:48:06,350
-My Suzerain.

1522
00:48:06,383 --> 00:48:08,487
-There is a spaceship
descending on Ophecius.

1523
00:48:08,520 --> 00:48:09,988
-It's Rocky Jones.

1524
00:48:10,022 --> 00:48:10,988
Please listen to him.

1525
00:48:11,022 --> 00:48:12,055
-Silence, Trinka.

1526
00:48:12,088 --> 00:48:13,925
My Suzerain does not need
the advice of a traitor.

1527
00:48:16,862 --> 00:48:20,898
[IMITATING LONE
RANGER THEME MUSIC]

1528
00:48:26,237 --> 00:48:28,207
-Atlasan, prepare to fire.

1529
00:48:28,240 --> 00:48:28,940
-You're fired.

1530
00:48:28,973 --> 00:48:29,373
Oh.

1531
00:48:35,180 --> 00:48:36,147
-Fire controls ready.

1532
00:48:36,180 --> 00:48:36,582
-No, Atlasan!

1533
00:48:39,417 --> 00:48:40,352
-Fire!

1534
00:48:40,385 --> 00:48:42,320
[ROCKET FIRED]

1535
00:48:42,353 --> 00:48:42,887
-Whoa!

1536
00:48:42,920 --> 00:48:45,623
Almost hit the string.

1537
00:48:45,657 --> 00:48:47,225
-That's heavy stuff
they're throwing, Rocky.

1538
00:48:47,258 --> 00:48:48,260
-Who care.

1539
00:48:48,293 --> 00:48:49,060
Gee, we might die.

1540
00:48:49,093 --> 00:48:51,128
Oh, boy.

1541
00:48:51,162 --> 00:48:53,398
-The next one will do it.

1542
00:48:53,432 --> 00:48:54,900
Ready, Atlasan.

1543
00:48:54,933 --> 00:48:57,168
Ready and--

1544
00:48:57,202 --> 00:48:57,668
-Whoop!

1545
00:48:57,702 --> 00:48:58,837
-Please, Atlasan.

1546
00:48:58,870 --> 00:49:01,072
Don't start to fire again,
or I shall have to kill you.

1547
00:49:01,105 --> 00:49:02,073
-"Thelma and Louise," 1999.

1548
00:49:02,107 --> 00:49:03,608
-Fire, Atlasan.

1549
00:49:03,642 --> 00:49:04,542
-Yes, my Suzerain.

1550
00:49:04,575 --> 00:49:05,710
-Then this will stop you.

1551
00:49:05,743 --> 00:49:06,577
-What a wingspan.

1552
00:49:06,610 --> 00:49:09,147
-Don't repeat the
order, Cleolanta.

1553
00:49:09,180 --> 00:49:11,282
-She's got one look,
and this is it.

1554
00:49:11,315 --> 00:49:12,150
-Hm.

1555
00:49:12,183 --> 00:49:14,652
-Friends are
visiting from Europe.

1556
00:49:14,685 --> 00:49:17,022
-Watch out for the tricycle!

1557
00:49:17,055 --> 00:49:18,323
Oh!

1558
00:49:18,357 --> 00:49:20,158
Oh!

1559
00:49:20,192 --> 00:49:23,728
-You hit my tricycle!

1560
00:49:23,762 --> 00:49:27,132
-Lasvon, imprison that woman.

1561
00:49:27,165 --> 00:49:29,267
-Yes ma'am, live to serve ya!

1562
00:49:29,300 --> 00:49:31,403
-Atlasan!

1563
00:49:31,437 --> 00:49:35,040
-There's ham in the fridge,
honey, and there's--

1564
00:49:35,073 --> 00:49:37,242
-15 years and just
never know, do ya?

1565
00:49:37,275 --> 00:49:39,310
Hm!

1566
00:49:39,343 --> 00:49:41,345
-Not since "Fire
Maidens of Outer Space"

1567
00:49:41,378 --> 00:49:44,215
has there been such a
ladder scene so compelling.

1568
00:49:44,248 --> 00:49:45,517
[GROANING]

1569
00:49:48,520 --> 00:49:51,557
-Super City, you
build it, by Marx.

1570
00:49:51,590 --> 00:49:52,290
-My hip broke.

1571
00:49:52,323 --> 00:49:54,458
-Hey, uh, Rocky,
have ya ever had

1572
00:49:54,492 --> 00:49:56,562
a funny feeling you're
about to get slugged?

1573
00:49:56,595 --> 00:49:57,695
-Here, let me
complete the thought.

1574
00:49:57,728 --> 00:49:58,628
Boom!

1575
00:49:58,662 --> 00:50:01,500
-No matter what happens,
Winky, don't fire.

1576
00:50:01,533 --> 00:50:02,300
-Hey, I'm new.

1577
00:50:02,333 --> 00:50:02,700
I'm Ralph.

1578
00:50:05,803 --> 00:50:08,173
-Oh, no! "Crash of
the Moons" is on!

1579
00:50:08,207 --> 00:50:10,242
-Mm, mm, mm.

1580
00:50:10,275 --> 00:50:11,375
-Alert the guards.

1581
00:50:11,408 --> 00:50:13,545
-Uh, w-we are guards.

1582
00:50:13,578 --> 00:50:15,713
-I don't want them inside
the city spreading lies

1583
00:50:15,747 --> 00:50:17,648
to my people about
the United Worlds.

1584
00:50:20,752 --> 00:50:23,488
-She's wearing that arm band
because her career is dead.

1585
00:50:23,522 --> 00:50:25,390
-Mm, hm.

1586
00:50:25,423 --> 00:50:27,258
-So that's when I
got into stamps.

1587
00:50:27,292 --> 00:50:27,758
It's fun.

1588
00:50:30,628 --> 00:50:32,463
-Well, I don't see
any welcome mat.

1589
00:50:32,497 --> 00:50:33,865
There isn't even a doorbell.

1590
00:50:33,898 --> 00:50:35,667
At least, when we were
here with Secretary Drake,

1591
00:50:35,700 --> 00:50:36,735
they let us in.

1592
00:50:36,768 --> 00:50:39,838
-Winky, I want to
hit you so hard.

1593
00:50:39,872 --> 00:50:40,738
-Hello!

1594
00:50:40,772 --> 00:50:43,208
It's important that
we see Cleolanta.

1595
00:50:43,242 --> 00:50:45,210
-Who is it that wishes
to see Cleolanta?

1596
00:50:45,243 --> 00:50:46,578
-Uh, we're selling candy.

1597
00:50:46,612 --> 00:50:49,815
Send boys like us to Jupiter.

1598
00:50:49,848 --> 00:50:52,617
-Oh, they've got, uh, no
visible panty line, there.

1599
00:50:52,650 --> 00:50:55,653
-Climb every cheap set,
till you find a plot.

1600
00:50:58,957 --> 00:51:01,192
-Come on, in or out
you space pilots.

1601
00:51:01,225 --> 00:51:02,393
We're not trying to
heat the outside.

1602
00:51:04,963 --> 00:51:06,330
-Ope, see, I told
ya we shouldn't

1603
00:51:06,363 --> 00:51:09,533
have put those things there.

1604
00:51:09,567 --> 00:51:12,870
-(SINGING) Da-da da, da,
da, da-da-da, da, duh.

1605
00:51:12,903 --> 00:51:13,872
Brrp, brrp.

1606
00:51:13,905 --> 00:51:15,440
-Hold it.

1607
00:51:15,473 --> 00:51:16,307
You all right, Winky?

1608
00:51:16,340 --> 00:51:16,775
-Sure, Skipper.

1609
00:51:16,808 --> 00:51:17,342
-All right.

1610
00:51:17,375 --> 00:51:18,910
Take us to Cleolanta.

1611
00:51:18,943 --> 00:51:19,477
Move!

1612
00:51:19,510 --> 00:51:20,478
-Take us to the river.

1613
00:51:20,512 --> 00:51:22,847
Drop us in the water.

1614
00:51:22,880 --> 00:51:24,883
-Huh, 2, 3, 4.

1615
00:51:24,917 --> 00:51:25,917
Huh--

1616
00:51:25,950 --> 00:51:27,352
--(SINGING CADENCE) We
are in a crappy film.

1617
00:51:27,385 --> 00:51:29,287
-We are in a crappy film!

1618
00:51:29,320 --> 00:51:31,857
-Hup!

1619
00:51:31,890 --> 00:51:32,557
-All right, Winky.

1620
00:51:32,590 --> 00:51:34,625
-Drop 'em.

1621
00:51:34,658 --> 00:51:35,493
-Hm?

1622
00:51:35,527 --> 00:51:36,660
-Atlasan!

1623
00:51:36,693 --> 00:51:38,430
-Cleolanta, I don't-- I--
I don't know what happened.

1624
00:51:38,463 --> 00:51:39,430
I was going down the--

1625
00:51:39,463 --> 00:51:41,967
-Cleolanta, you're going
to sit down and listen

1626
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:43,868
to every word I have to say.

1627
00:51:43,902 --> 00:51:45,737
-Sure, it's for your own good.

1628
00:51:45,770 --> 00:51:50,008
-You're going to sit down and
think about what you've done.

1629
00:51:50,042 --> 00:51:51,577
-Next, on "Nick at Night."

1630
00:51:51,610 --> 00:51:52,643
-Come on, bring it in.

1631
00:51:52,677 --> 00:51:54,345
Come on, bring it--
you're doing OK.

1632
00:51:54,378 --> 00:51:54,880
[BABY FUSSING]

1633
00:51:54,913 --> 00:51:55,713
[CLICKING TONGUE]

1634
00:51:55,747 --> 00:51:57,415
-Baby trapped in
film eats own hand.

1635
00:51:57,448 --> 00:51:58,583
News at 11:00.

1636
00:51:58,617 --> 00:52:00,952
-And he's been so
happy for days.

1637
00:52:00,985 --> 00:52:03,455
Laughing, and not
a single whimper.

1638
00:52:03,488 --> 00:52:05,457
-Now he insists on eating.

1639
00:52:05,490 --> 00:52:06,692
-Yes, Mr. Secretary.

1640
00:52:06,725 --> 00:52:08,460
-This toaster speaks to me.

1641
00:52:08,493 --> 00:52:11,563
-Yes, I'll-- I'll
tell her, at once.

1642
00:52:11,597 --> 00:52:14,365
Oh, and my very best regards--

1643
00:52:14,398 --> 00:52:15,667
-What a nut burger!

1644
00:52:15,700 --> 00:52:17,802
-And to Torvak.

1645
00:52:17,835 --> 00:52:19,070
Out.

1646
00:52:19,103 --> 00:52:21,338
-Alfred, to the bat cave.

1647
00:52:21,372 --> 00:52:22,907
-I just talked into
the radio antenna.

1648
00:52:22,940 --> 00:52:23,942
Everything's fine.

1649
00:52:23,975 --> 00:52:25,310
[BABY CRYING]

1650
00:52:25,343 --> 00:52:25,910
-Vena--

1651
00:52:25,943 --> 00:52:27,077
-Shut that kid up!

1652
00:52:27,110 --> 00:52:28,847
-The meeting on Nagato has
been successfully completed.

1653
00:52:28,880 --> 00:52:30,582
-Domo Arigato, Mr. Roboto.

1654
00:52:30,615 --> 00:52:33,852
-Torvak will gladly welcome the
unfortunate people of Posita

1655
00:52:33,885 --> 00:52:34,285
to his moon.

1656
00:52:34,318 --> 00:52:35,185
[BABY CRYING]

1657
00:52:35,218 --> 00:52:37,488
-Oh, but, uh, when
will Bavarro return?

1658
00:52:37,522 --> 00:52:38,022
-Coo-coo.
Coo-coo.

1659
00:52:38,055 --> 00:52:38,722
Coo-coo.

1660
00:52:38,755 --> 00:52:41,458
-And I have concern for our son.

1661
00:52:41,492 --> 00:52:43,027
-He bit me, the
little son of a--

1662
00:52:43,060 --> 00:52:46,865
-They are making plans for
temporary housing on Nagato,

1663
00:52:46,898 --> 00:52:48,800
so we can start the evacuation.

1664
00:52:48,833 --> 00:52:50,368
-Ew!

1665
00:52:50,402 --> 00:52:51,602
-All right, we're
going to go out there

1666
00:52:51,635 --> 00:52:53,605
and we're going to show this
team what we've got, all right?

1667
00:52:53,638 --> 00:52:55,740
-No, Cleolanta, not
a day must be wasted.

1668
00:52:55,773 --> 00:52:57,575
Not even a single hour.

1669
00:52:57,608 --> 00:52:58,575
-So lunch?

1670
00:52:58,608 --> 00:53:00,978
-Winky and I will return
to Posita immediately

1671
00:53:01,012 --> 00:53:02,880
to help with their evacuation.

1672
00:53:02,913 --> 00:53:04,082
-But what about Ophecius?

1673
00:53:04,115 --> 00:53:05,550
(MOCKINGLY) What about Ophecius?

1674
00:53:05,583 --> 00:53:07,818
- --will be dispatched
from the United Worlds.

1675
00:53:07,852 --> 00:53:10,055
They'll help you with your
evacuation to a new world.

1676
00:53:10,088 --> 00:53:10,922
-Yuck.

1677
00:53:10,955 --> 00:53:13,023
-Which will be
mutually agreed upon.

1678
00:53:13,057 --> 00:53:15,627
-They will tell me
where to take my people?

1679
00:53:15,660 --> 00:53:16,160
-Hm!

1680
00:53:16,193 --> 00:53:17,128
-No, Cleolanta.

1681
00:53:17,162 --> 00:53:18,797
They'll only advise.

1682
00:53:18,830 --> 00:53:19,932
-For you!

1683
00:53:19,965 --> 00:53:21,867
-Please!

1684
00:53:21,900 --> 00:53:24,502
-Jeez, the Paris Peace
Talks were easier than this.

1685
00:53:24,535 --> 00:53:26,938
-Let me speak, alone,
with my lieutenants,

1686
00:53:26,972 --> 00:53:28,507
Atlasan and Lasvon.

1687
00:53:28,540 --> 00:53:29,907
-You can tell they're
falling in love.

1688
00:53:29,940 --> 00:53:31,610
You can see the sparks.

1689
00:53:31,643 --> 00:53:32,177
-Mm, hm.

1690
00:53:32,210 --> 00:53:33,512
-All right, Cleolanta.

1691
00:53:33,545 --> 00:53:35,080
-I'm feeling stupid today.

1692
00:53:41,653 --> 00:53:42,320
-Cleolanta!

1693
00:53:42,353 --> 00:53:44,522
-I'm just going to put pre-heat.

1694
00:53:44,555 --> 00:53:45,957
-They must be silenced.

1695
00:53:45,990 --> 00:53:47,958
If word of the crash
of moons leaked out,

1696
00:53:47,992 --> 00:53:49,660
there'd be panic
here on Ophecius.

1697
00:53:49,693 --> 00:53:51,195
-We can't imagine why.

1698
00:53:51,228 --> 00:53:52,462
-Mm, mm.

1699
00:53:52,495 --> 00:53:56,968
-The gas will keep them inactive
until I've decided what to do.

1700
00:53:57,002 --> 00:53:58,903
-[SNIFFING] Winky, you
been eating cabbage?

1701
00:53:58,937 --> 00:54:00,572
-What is it?

1702
00:54:00,605 --> 00:54:04,275
-Quick, Winky, cover your face.

1703
00:54:04,308 --> 00:54:06,812
-No, no, more of your face!

1704
00:54:06,845 --> 00:54:08,747
-The vent, up there.

1705
00:54:08,780 --> 00:54:09,880
-No, that's the sconce.

1706
00:54:13,283 --> 00:54:14,918
-Come with me, Atlasan.

1707
00:54:14,952 --> 00:54:16,287
We will make our own plans.

1708
00:54:16,320 --> 00:54:16,922
-Heh, heh, heh.

1709
00:54:32,603 --> 00:54:33,670
-Hm?

1710
00:54:33,703 --> 00:54:36,908
-To be safe, Atlasan, we
should explode Posita, here.

1711
00:54:36,942 --> 00:54:38,843
-If we exploded it
there, Posita wouldn't

1712
00:54:38,877 --> 00:54:41,345
have a chance to
evacuate all its people.

1713
00:54:41,378 --> 00:54:42,412
-Pshaw!

1714
00:54:42,445 --> 00:54:46,183
-This vagrant moon,
Posita, aims to destroy us.

1715
00:54:46,217 --> 00:54:49,020
Instead, we will destroy it.

1716
00:54:49,053 --> 00:54:51,022
We act only for
self-preservation.

1717
00:54:51,055 --> 00:54:52,157
-We're Republicans.

1718
00:54:52,190 --> 00:54:52,957
-Yes, my Suzerain.

1719
00:54:52,990 --> 00:54:54,458
-You're wearing
the crown, honey.

1720
00:54:58,328 --> 00:54:58,930
-Hm?

1721
00:55:01,332 --> 00:55:02,667
-Oh, the cookies are done.

1722
00:55:02,700 --> 00:55:03,768
Tollhouse!

1723
00:55:03,802 --> 00:55:07,005
[SNORING]

1724
00:55:07,038 --> 00:55:08,373
-The trail, becomes her.

1725
00:55:08,407 --> 00:55:10,142
Hm, hm.

1726
00:55:10,175 --> 00:55:13,010
-It's the extermination
room at the Fanta Suites.

1727
00:55:13,043 --> 00:55:14,378
-Hm?

1728
00:55:14,412 --> 00:55:15,647
Oon yellimon!

1729
00:55:15,680 --> 00:55:19,383
Oon yel-- uh, huh?

1730
00:55:19,417 --> 00:55:19,950
-Heh, heh, heh,.

1731
00:55:19,983 --> 00:55:21,720
This is my lucky day.

1732
00:55:26,123 --> 00:55:29,427
-So, um, are you still sore
at me for turning you in?

1733
00:55:29,460 --> 00:55:31,095
Uh, hm?

1734
00:55:31,128 --> 00:55:31,930
Lamb chop!

1735
00:55:31,963 --> 00:55:33,330
Pumpkin!

1736
00:55:33,363 --> 00:55:34,265
Snooker!

1737
00:55:34,298 --> 00:55:35,733
-Trinka.

1738
00:55:35,767 --> 00:55:37,302
Trinka!

1739
00:55:37,335 --> 00:55:37,835
-Trinka.

1740
00:55:37,868 --> 00:55:39,337
Trinka, Trinka, doo!

1741
00:55:39,370 --> 00:55:42,473
-Atlasan, tell me we're home.

1742
00:55:42,507 --> 00:55:44,075
I had such a bad dream.

1743
00:55:44,108 --> 00:55:46,477
I want to hear you
laugh and say, wake up.

1744
00:55:46,510 --> 00:55:47,378
Forget your dreams.

1745
00:55:47,412 --> 00:55:48,980
-Yeah, forget your dreams.

1746
00:55:49,013 --> 00:55:52,017
You're in prison, honey.

1747
00:55:52,050 --> 00:55:54,152
-But, Trinka, I did only what I
thought was right for Ophecius.

1748
00:55:54,185 --> 00:55:54,785
-Oh.

1749
00:55:54,818 --> 00:55:56,822
-Did you kill Rocky Jones?

1750
00:55:56,855 --> 00:55:57,388
-No.

1751
00:55:57,422 --> 00:55:59,190
No, he's only asleep.

1752
00:55:59,223 --> 00:56:01,325
-Atlasan, did he get
a chance to speak?

1753
00:56:01,358 --> 00:56:02,525
-Yes, Trinka.

1754
00:56:02,558 --> 00:56:06,330
And now I'll be a great man
in the history of Ophecius.

1755
00:56:06,363 --> 00:56:07,765
The savior of our planet.

1756
00:56:07,798 --> 00:56:09,000
-Hm, hm.

1757
00:56:09,033 --> 00:56:09,567
-How?

1758
00:56:09,600 --> 00:56:10,902
-Uh, I-- I don't know.

1759
00:56:10,935 --> 00:56:11,935
- --on a spaceship.

1760
00:56:11,968 --> 00:56:15,540
We leave soon to intercept
it's menacing moon.

1761
00:56:15,573 --> 00:56:17,808
It will be my honor to
fire tritanic missiles

1762
00:56:17,842 --> 00:56:20,778
into Posita, which
was save Ophecius.

1763
00:56:20,812 --> 00:56:21,947
-I love it when
you talk that way.

1764
00:56:21,980 --> 00:56:23,548
-I'll give the order, Trinka.

1765
00:56:23,582 --> 00:56:25,850
And all I ask for
is a full pardon.

1766
00:56:25,883 --> 00:56:26,952
-Do I have to quit my job?

1767
00:56:26,985 --> 00:56:27,785
-They're looking for you.

1768
00:56:27,818 --> 00:56:29,520
-But on the
astrophone, Rocky Jones

1769
00:56:29,553 --> 00:56:31,355
said there are
people on this moon.

1770
00:56:31,388 --> 00:56:32,590
-Trinka, that can't be helped.

1771
00:56:32,623 --> 00:56:33,423
-Atlasan.

1772
00:56:33,457 --> 00:56:33,990
-Hm?

1773
00:56:34,023 --> 00:56:35,393
-Report to landing base.

1774
00:56:35,427 --> 00:56:35,960
-Goodbye, Trinka.

1775
00:56:35,993 --> 00:56:37,328
-Boy, her voice carries.

1776
00:56:37,362 --> 00:56:38,463
-Wait.

1777
00:56:38,497 --> 00:56:39,997
Warn those people on Posita.

1778
00:56:40,030 --> 00:56:41,030
Give them a chance to live.

1779
00:56:41,063 --> 00:56:43,835
-Trinka, I'm only obeying
Cleolanta's orders.

1780
00:56:43,868 --> 00:56:45,237
-I vas in Austria during da var!

1781
00:56:45,270 --> 00:56:47,138
-- --his life to warn us.

1782
00:56:47,172 --> 00:56:49,140
-Well, why don't you
marry Rocky Jones then?

1783
00:56:49,173 --> 00:56:51,042
-We must do the same for others.

1784
00:56:51,075 --> 00:56:52,943
-Atlasan, report
to landing base!

1785
00:56:52,977 --> 00:56:54,878
-I'm coming, you great cow!

1786
00:56:54,912 --> 00:56:57,882
0 go back to sleep, and
know nothing until I return.

1787
00:56:57,915 --> 00:56:59,350
-Sorry about your
death sentence, hun.

1788
00:56:59,383 --> 00:57:01,285
Bye bye.

1789
00:57:01,318 --> 00:57:03,588
-Uh, hun, would you
turn on the gas again?

1790
00:57:03,622 --> 00:57:04,522
I'm tired.

1791
00:57:04,555 --> 00:57:06,323
Thanks a lot.

1792
00:57:06,357 --> 00:57:09,127
-One more look!

1793
00:57:09,160 --> 00:57:11,095
-Hey, she's flipping me off!

1794
00:57:11,128 --> 00:57:11,495
Huh!

1795
00:57:11,528 --> 00:57:12,130
That gal.

1796
00:57:16,467 --> 00:57:19,970
-Whoa, did I get really
betrayed last night, or what?

1797
00:57:25,008 --> 00:57:25,875
-Oh, hi.

1798
00:57:25,908 --> 00:57:27,345
I was just coming to
fluff your pillow.

1799
00:57:27,378 --> 00:57:29,480
-Trinka, you're a
great deal wiser

1800
00:57:29,513 --> 00:57:32,117
than I am, and much favored.

1801
00:57:32,150 --> 00:57:34,685
You do whatever you think is
best, but please be careful.

1802
00:57:34,718 --> 00:57:37,588
Lasvon is on guard, and
he thinks you're asleep.

1803
00:57:37,622 --> 00:57:38,557
[APPROACHING FOOTSTEPS]

1804
00:57:38,590 --> 00:57:39,490
-Get in!

1805
00:57:39,523 --> 00:57:41,658
-Oh, I'm never going
to get to kiss her!

1806
00:57:44,495 --> 00:57:45,730
-All right, a hundred
bucks to whoever

1807
00:57:45,763 --> 00:57:47,098
